# --- s046 Book I d.13 q.un. = Ord. I d.13 q.un.
n("n746","s046-01","Circa distinctionem decimam tertiam","la","source","= Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 13 q. un., *utrum productio Spiritus Sancti sit generatio* (Vat. V). Scotus also reviews and rejects several ways of distinguishing the productions.","to-verify")
n("n747","s046-01","Generatio et modus","la","textual","Thus A. The argument (*ergo vnus motus*) and Aristotle, *Phys.* V 1 (224b7–10, motions are distinguished by their *termini ad quem*), require *motus*. The translation reads ‘motion’.","conjecture")
n("n748","s046-01","Aug. 5. de trini. c. 17.","la","source","Augustine, *De Trin.* V 14.15: *exiit enim, non quomodo natus, sed quomodo datus; et ideo non dicitur filius*. Gorris's ‘c. 17’ again (compare 039, 041).","certain")
n("n749","s046-02","Prima est Egidii","la","source","Giles of Rome, *In I Sent.* d. 13 (article 2 as cited): the processions are distinguished by their terms.","to-verify")
n("n750","s046-02","fratris Guillermi varronis","la","historical","William of Ware OFM, *In I Sent.* d. 13. Here A spells the name clearly (compare 044-02).","certain")
n("n751","s046-02","q. 35. articulo. 2°.","la","source","Probably Aquinas, *ST* I q. 36 a. 2 ad 7 (the Son is from one, the Spirit from two). For *q. 35* compare 043.","to-verify")
n("n752","s046-02","Godofredi de fontibus","la","source","Godfrey of Fontaines, *Quodl.* III q. 3, as printed. The locus is to be checked.","to-verify")
n("n753","s046-02","q. 27. articulo. 4.","la","source","Aquinas, *ST* I q. 27 a. 4 ad 1 (*utrum processio amoris sit generatio*).","to-verify")
n("n754","s046-02","Henrici in summa articulo. 27. q. 7.","la","source","Henry of Ghent, *Summa*, as printed (a. 27 q. 7). Henry's doctrine of distinction by the elicitive principles (intellect and will) is mainly in *Summa* a. 54 and a. 60. The numeral may be corrupt.","uncertain")
n("n755","s046-02","quodlibeto. 5. q. 1.","la","source","Henry of Ghent, *Quodl.* V q. 1 (nature and will as the principles of the productions); cf. 039.","to-verify")
n("n756","s046-02","fratris Ade","la","historical","‘Brother Adam’, *I Sent.* d. 6 q. 1 a. 2. This is probably Adam Wodeham OFM (d. 1358), or possibly another Adam. A post-Scotistic authority added by Gorris; not in Scotus.","uncertain")
n("n757","s046-03","productiones distinguuntur seipsis formaliter","la","source","Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 13 q. un.: the productions are distinguished by themselves formally (*se ipsis formaliter*), and by their principles (nature and will) as by their elicitive *rationes*.","to-verify")
n("n758","s046-03","Aug. 15. de tri.","la","source","Augustine, *De Trin.* XV 27.50: *quantum distet nativitas verbi a processione doni*… *ut voluntatem de cognitione procedere… non tamen eius esse imaginem*. Gorris reads *dati* for *doni*.","to-verify")
n("n759","s046-03","Cur spiritus sanctus non sit filius","la","source","Augustine, *De Trin.* V 14.15.","certain")
n("n760","s046-05","aliqua res est infinita in se et a se","la","source","Threefold classification: infinite *in se et a se* (Father), infinite *in se* but not *a se* (Son, Spirit), finite (creature). Cf. Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 13 (on the *infinitas* of the produced persons).","to-verify")
n("n761","s046-05","ypostatice","la","translation","‘Hypostatically’, i.e. as a person (*hypostasis*), as against *substantialiter* (the common essence).","certain")
n("n762","s046-01","motion","en","translation","A prints *modus*; translated as *motus*. See Latin note.")
n("n763","s046-04","argumentatively","en","translation","*argutive*: in the order of argument or knowledge (*innotescunt*), as against *quidditative* and *elicitive*.")

# --- B collation (full): B64L–B65R
upd("n747", append=" B also has *modus* (*Generatio et modus distinguuntur preter modos*), so the error is common to both printings.")
upd("n748", append=" B also *v. de tri. ca. xvij.*")
upd("n751", append=" B also *q. xxxv. arti. ij.*")
n("n987","s046-03","secundum Aug. 5. de tri. c. 17","la","textual","B: *secundum Augustinum v. de trini. capitulo iij.*","certain")
n("n988","s046-03","integre distanciam","la","textual","B: *intelligi distantiam*.","certain")
n("n989","s046-03","Idem. 5. de tri. c. 17.","la","textual","B: *Item. v. de trini. ca. xxiij.* A's *c. 17* agrees with its other citations of the passage.","certain")
n("n990","s046-04","et tamen sunt seipsis primo formaliter distincte","la","textual","B: *et non sunt seipsis…*, which contradicts the argument; A is right.","certain")
